{
  "case_id": "2024-24-304",
  "document_hash": "fe7c353a4d6a787d6c64e9a236efb85b94f86b44896533fc721664eea07b2d13",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2024-24-304",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fe7c353a4d6a787d6c64e9a236efb85b94f86b44896533fc721664eea07b2d13",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fe7c353a4d6a-0000-0002",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "APPEARANCES: NOEL J. FRANCISCO, ESQUIRE, Washington, D.C.; on behalf of the Petitioner. SOPAN JOSHI, Assistant to the Solicitor General, Department of Justice, Washington, D.C.; for the United States, as amicus curiae, supporting neither party. DEEPAK GUPTA, ESQUIRE, Washington, D.C.; on behalf of the Respondents."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Laboratory Corporation of America (Petitioner)",
      "case_id": "2024-24-304",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fe7c353a4d6a787d6c64e9a236efb85b94f86b44896533fc721664eea07b2d13",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fe7c353a4d6a-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. FRANCISCO: Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court: Two basic principles resolve this case. First, a class action is just a tool for aggregating claims. So, if an individual plaintiff doesn't have Article III standing to bring his own claim, he can't bring it as part of a class either. That's why Laroe held that an intervenor has to show Article III standing in order to intervene, and, as Justice Scalia said in Shady Grove, class actions are just another species of joinder. Second, Rule 23(b)(3)'s predominance requirement leads to the same result. If a class is defined to include plaintiffs without Article III standing and, as a result, you need thousands of mini-trials to separate the wheat"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Laboratory Corporation of America (Petitioner)",
      "case_id": "2024-24-304",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fe7c353a4d6a787d6c64e9a236efb85b94f86b44896533fc721664eea07b2d13",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fe7c353a4d6a-0000-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Plaintiffs who don't want to use kiosks don't have standing to challenge how kiosks work any more than a vegan has standing to challenge how a restaurant defines a medium rare steak. As a result, the Court needs to assess whether each of the 8,000 to 112,000 class members actually want to use kiosks, and that will necessarily swamp any common issues, as the D.C. and First Circuits correctly held in the Rail Freight and Asacol cases."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2024-24-304",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fe7c353a4d6a787d6c64e9a236efb85b94f86b44896533fc721664eea07b2d13",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fe7c353a4d6a-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 7,
        "start": 7
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE THOMAS: The -- in this case, there have been a number of orders, and it seems as though the one that we have before us is the May order, which is inoperative. Would you spend a minute on why we still -- we have jurisdiction over the May order when there have been subsequent orders?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2024-24-304",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fe7c353a4d6a787d6c64e9a236efb85b94f86b44896533fc721664eea07b2d13",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fe7c353a4d6a-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "So, as I said, you're not going to have a class action if your definition is are you going to have a thousand mini-trials."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2024-24-304",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fe7c353a4d6a787d6c64e9a236efb85b94f86b44896533fc721664eea07b2d13",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fe7c353a4d6a-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 30,
        "start": 30
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "You've probably covered this at some point, but could you just spend a minute on why the May class definition includes so many uninjured --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Francisco",
      "case_id": "2024-24-304",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fe7c353a4d6a787d6c64e9a236efb85b94f86b44896533fc721664eea07b2d13",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fe7c353a4d6a-0001-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 31,
        "start": 31
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "class reads is it says anybody who -- you know, it kind of parrots the language of the statute. But their understanding of the language of the statute that the district court adopted was that that includes anybody who walked into the facility."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2024-24-304",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fe7c353a4d6a787d6c64e9a236efb85b94f86b44896533fc721664eea07b2d13",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fe7c353a4d6a-0001-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 36,
        "start": 36
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I'm troubled by the Ninth Circuit's rule that a new notice of appeal must be filed or a prior notice of appeal must be amended if the district court, while a class certification appeal is pending in the court of appeals, makes a material change in the class certification but, presumably, not if the district court makes an immaterial change."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2024-24-304",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fe7c353a4d6a787d6c64e9a236efb85b94f86b44896533fc721664eea07b2d13",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fe7c353a4d6a-0001-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The -- the -- this Court has said that non-named parties are parties for some purposes but not for other purposes. And I know you want us to hold that they must be parties for Article III purposes."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2024-24-304",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fe7c353a4d6a787d6c64e9a236efb85b94f86b44896533fc721664eea07b2d13",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fe7c353a4d6a-0001-0007",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "When does a party become -- when does a party become a part of a litigation."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Francisco",
      "case_id": "2024-24-304",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fe7c353a4d6a787d6c64e9a236efb85b94f86b44896533fc721664eea07b2d13",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fe7c353a4d6a-0002-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "If they lose, if the class is certified and they lose, the entire class is bound by that adverse judgment."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Francisco",
      "case_id": "2024-24-304",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fe7c353a4d6a787d6c64e9a236efb85b94f86b44896533fc721664eea07b2d13",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fe7c353a4d6a-0002-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 55,
        "start": 55
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I think that just illustrates the nature of the problem. I think that just reflects the fundamental principles of Article III jurisdiction."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Barrett",
      "case_id": "2024-24-304",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fe7c353a4d6a787d6c64e9a236efb85b94f86b44896533fc721664eea07b2d13",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fe7c353a4d6a-0002-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 67,
        "start": 67
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Do you follow me? Am I being clear?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2024-24-304",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fe7c353a4d6a787d6c64e9a236efb85b94f86b44896533fc721664eea07b2d13",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fe7c353a4d6a-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 69,
        "start": 69
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Justice Alito pointed out this is a weird, not clear rule from the Ninth Circuit. So I'm trying to figure out what the consequence to your client would be if some of those concerns carried the day."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Francisco",
      "case_id": "2024-24-304",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fe7c353a4d6a787d6c64e9a236efb85b94f86b44896533fc721664eea07b2d13",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fe7c353a4d6a-0003-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 70,
        "start": 70
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Under Rule 23(f), we are way past the 14-day period to appeal the August order. So there would have to be then some other -- some kind of equitable tolling concept that gets built into and on top of that. And, as I said, if you were to do that -- and -- and I would strongly urge you not to -- I would be vigorously arguing for anything I could think of to allow us to appeal that August order well past the 14-day period of limitations under 28(f), and I would do my best to succeed."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Sopan Joshi",
      "case_id": "2024-24-304",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fe7c353a4d6a787d6c64e9a236efb85b94f86b44896533fc721664eea07b2d13",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fe7c353a4d6a-0003-0002",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 84,
        "start": 84
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "This Court has frequently said that Rule 23 requires all class members to share the same injury. We think that includes an Article III injury."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2024-24-304",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fe7c353a4d6a787d6c64e9a236efb85b94f86b44896533fc721664eea07b2d13",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fe7c353a4d6a-0003-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 85,
        "start": 85
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE THOMAS: So what would you do at the early stages of the litigation, say, post-certification, and -- and you find injured -- uninjured parties in the -- in the class?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2024-24-304",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fe7c353a4d6a787d6c64e9a236efb85b94f86b44896533fc721664eea07b2d13",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fe7c353a4d6a-0003-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 86,
        "start": 86
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GORSUCH: Why would that be the case, though? Because you have uninjured people in the party that you've now found. Why"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2024-24-304",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fe7c353a4d6a787d6c64e9a236efb85b94f86b44896533fc721664eea07b2d13",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fe7c353a4d6a-0004-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 90,
        "start": 90
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GORSUCH: So an Article III injury is required? It's a backdoor way of getting to Petitioner's position, I think."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Jackson",
      "case_id": "2024-24-304",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fe7c353a4d6a787d6c64e9a236efb85b94f86b44896533fc721664eea07b2d13",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fe7c353a4d6a-0004-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 92,
        "start": 92
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE JACKSON: But, Mr. Joshi, when we look at commonality and predominance, and the treatises say this, they don't pick out a particular issue and say you have to have that."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2024-24-304",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fe7c353a4d6a787d6c64e9a236efb85b94f86b44896533fc721664eea07b2d13",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fe7c353a4d6a-0004-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 110,
        "start": 110
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAVANAUGH: When you said Rule 23 is narrower than Article III, I just want to make sure I understand how you think it's narrower."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2024-24-304",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fe7c353a4d6a787d6c64e9a236efb85b94f86b44896533fc721664eea07b2d13",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fe7c353a4d6a-0005-0003",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 114,
        "start": 114
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "As this Court held in TransUnion and as the Chief Justice recognized in Tyson Foods, Article III doesn't give federal courts the power to give relief to any uninjured plaintiff, class action or not."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Federal jurisdiction professors",
      "case_id": "2024-24-304",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fe7c353a4d6a787d6c64e9a236efb85b94f86b44896533fc721664eea07b2d13",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fe7c353a4d6a-0005-0002",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 116,
        "start": 116
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the amicus brief of the federal jurisdiction professors indicates, there were a number of ways in which the petition obscured this jurisdictional problem."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Gupta",
      "case_id": "2024-24-304",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fe7c353a4d6a787d6c64e9a236efb85b94f86b44896533fc721664eea07b2d13",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fe7c353a4d6a-0006-0000",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 132,
        "start": 132
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the district court didn't have any battle over this and didn't certify a class that was premised on the idea that there was a contest over whether there were uninjured people."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Barrett",
      "case_id": "2024-24-304",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fe7c353a4d6a787d6c64e9a236efb85b94f86b44896533fc721664eea07b2d13",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fe7c353a4d6a-0006-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 132,
        "start": 132
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BARRETT: Well, Mr. Gupta, that -- that's the question that we didn't get to in Acheson, right? There are arguments that racial discrimination and other kinds of discrimination are different."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Barrett",
      "case_id": "2024-24-304",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fe7c353a4d6a787d6c64e9a236efb85b94f86b44896533fc721664eea07b2d13",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fe7c353a4d6a-0006-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 135,
        "start": 135
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BARRETT: But like what -- but what you're saying -- I mean, because I don't want to take up your time, and you can divert it. Like, just what you're saying is that it would be impossible -- if -- if -- if we agree with you on kind of the Acheson-esque point, you're saying it would be impossible for everyone in the class not to have standing, as you describe it, so that this would just kind of be irrelevant?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2024-24-304",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fe7c353a4d6a787d6c64e9a236efb85b94f86b44896533fc721664eea07b2d13",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fe7c353a4d6a-0006-0007",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 146,
        "start": 146
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: And he takes from that that if there's no time --if there's no clarity to the rule, then you can do it at any time. Do you think that's correct?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Jackson",
      "case_id": "2024-24-304",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fe7c353a4d6a787d6c64e9a236efb85b94f86b44896533fc721664eea07b2d13",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fe7c353a4d6a-0006-0009",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 150,
        "start": 150
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE JACKSON: One quick thing. You say the job is to weed out the uninjured. I think Mr. Francisco says you have to do that at the start by virtue of Article III and Rule 23. And the government joins him with respect to the second point of that. You seem to say it suffices just to know that there is going to be a mechanism to do that down the road eventually. Why is he wrong about the timing of this?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner (Noel J. Francisco)",
      "case_id": "2024-24-304",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fe7c353a4d6a787d6c64e9a236efb85b94f86b44896533fc721664eea07b2d13",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fe7c353a4d6a-0007-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 153,
        "start": 153
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. FRANCISCO: Thank you, Mr. Chief Justice. To begin with the procedural issue, here's what the district court said twice: In refining the class definition, this order does not materially alter the composition of the class or materially change in any manner the Heritage Reporting Corporation"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Plaintiffs",
      "case_id": "2024-24-304",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fe7c353a4d6a787d6c64e9a236efb85b94f86b44896533fc721664eea07b2d13",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fe7c353a4d6a-0007-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 154,
        "start": 154
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Here's what plaintiffs argued to the district court when it urged the district court to adopt the August definition. It moved to to recline -- to refine the class definition, and it assured the court that it was \"identical in every way to the original May definition.\" And it assured it that it had not changed the \"substance\" of the class."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2024-24-304",
